videos.script:
The planner wants to remind you of a study session. To do that, it needs your permission. {{ask}}

When it asks matters more than how. Ask the moment the app opens, before you have seen a single session, and most people say no. {{launch}} Ask when you tap remind me, and the question explains itself. {{context}}

And a no does not wait to be asked again. On Android, the second no is final: the dialog never comes back. {{android}} On iPhone, the first one is. {{ios}} After that, the only way back is the Settings app, and the person has to choose to go there.

Today you model one permission on both platforms, as their documentation describes it. {{model}} You feed it two kinds of app: one that asks at launch, and one that asks in context. Then you print what each may still do.
